{"seq":42,"at":"2026-10-23","kind":"reworded","target":{"type":"wording","id":"w14921"},"reason":"Goodall was not strictly 'the first' to name study animals: Japanese primatologists named individual macaques from the early 1950s (Imo, Koshima, 1953). The question now asks who broke with the numbering convention of her field; the card's words stay in cardText.","by":"provenance-research","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jane_Goodall"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hundredth_monkey_effect"}],"changes":[{"field":"en","old":"Which scientist was the first to give the subjects she studied names instead of the usual numbers?","new":"Which scientist broke with the convention of her field by giving the animals she studied names instead of the usual numbers?"},{"field":"de","old":"Welche Wissenschaftlerin war die erste, die den von ihr zu erforschenden Subjekten Namen gab, anstatt der sonst üblichen Zahlen?","new":"Welche Wissenschaftlerin brach mit der Konvention ihres Fachs, indem sie den von ihr erforschten Tieren Namen statt der üblichen Nummern gab?"},{"field":"ru","old":"Какая исследовательница первой стала давать изучаемым ею животным имена вместо обычных номеров?","new":"Какая исследовательница нарушила традицию своей науки, давая изучаемым животным имена вместо обычных номеров?"},{"field":"cardText","new":"Welche Wissenschaftlerin war die erste, die den von ihr zu erforschenden Subjekten Namen gab, anstatt der sonst üblichen Zahlen?"}],"hash":"52743d4d7d88","actor":{"kind":"agent","name":"provenance-research"},"run":"provenance-research-2026-10-23","chain":"c88f42e5cee0d490d63d5fda35f280937601e782dc0f8403b03d39dbb7682509"},
